   "source": [
    "**Concept:** LightGBM grows trees **leaf-wise** (best-loss-reduction leaf split next) rather than **level-wise** (every leaf at a depth splits before moving deeper, XGBoost's default). Leaf-wise can reach a lower loss with fewer splits, but it's easier to overfit on a small/noisy leaf if `num_leaves`/`min_data_in_leaf` aren't controlled — think about which of your Week 6/7 depth findings (shallow depth generally best, `min_samples_leaf` interacting with depth) this predicts for LightGBM's own controls.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Histogram binning:** continuous features are pre-bucketed into a fixed number of histogram bins before split-finding, which is why LightGBM is typically faster on large tabular datasets than XGBoost's exact or approximate split search."
   ]
